adjudication.rationale:
In `CalendarService.ts` a new awaited call was added:

```ts
// Update SelectedCalendar.updatedAt for all calendars under this credential
await SelectedCalendarRepository.updateManyByCredentialId(this.credential.id, {});
```

There is no `try/catch` or other error isolation around this auxiliary `updateMany` call, so any Prisma/DB error thrown here will propagate and fail the whole surrounding availability-related method execution. The diff shows this write is appended after cache-related work, and it is not guarded the way a “best-effort bookkeeping” update often would be. Whether it *must* be best-effort isn’t provable from the diff, so this is a concrete robustness concern rather than a definitively incorrect behavior.
